<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>救生艇新闻：博客——保护人类</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/</link><description></description><lastBuildDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:17:06 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>研究显示患有抑郁症的成年人新脑细胞形成停滞</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/new-brain-cell-formation-stalls-in-adults-with-depression-study-shows</link><description>一项新研究的发现&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/new-brain-cell-formation-stalls-in-adults-with-depression-study-shows2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:17:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/new-brain-cell-formation-stalls-in-adults-with-depression-study-shows</guid></item><item><title>超分辨率显微镜揭示抗癌药物如何触发细胞分解</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/super-resolution-microscopy-reveals-how-a-cancer-drug-triggers-cellular-breakdown</link><description>癌症药物通常被设计用来阻断特定的分子靶标，但它们进入细胞后发生的情况并不总是被很好地理解。一项新研究&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/super-resolution-microscopy-reveals-how-a-cancer-drug-triggers-cellular-breakdown2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:02:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/super-resolution-microscopy-reveals-how-a-cancer-drug-triggers-cellular-breakdown</guid></item><item><title>“梦想细胞”展览：在日常场景中观察细胞的艺术</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/dreaming-cells-exhibit-the-art-of-seeing-cells-in-everyday-scenes</link><description>神经科学家出身的科学插画家拉迪卡·帕特纳拉 (Radhika Patnala) 将细胞生物学转化为生动的风景，强调人体与自然之间的相似之处。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/dreaming-cells-exhibit-the-art-of-seeing-cells-in-everyday-scenes.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 11:47:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/dreaming-cells-exhibit-the-art-of-seeing-cells-in-everyday-scenes</guid></item><item><title>大型强子对撞机碰撞揭示了氧和氖核几何结构的变化</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/lhc-collisions-reveal-oxygen-and-neons-shifting-nuclear-geometry</link><description>许多人都知道，欧洲核子研究中心的大型强子对撞机 (LHC) 以接近光速的速度将微小的亚原子粒子粉碎在一起，以测试基本物理定律并发现新的基本粒子，但一些实验也可以帮助科学家更好地可视化我们已经熟悉的原子的实际结构，例如氧和氖。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/lhc-collisions-reveal-oxygen-and-neons-shifting-nuclear-geometry.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 11:32:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/lhc-collisions-reveal-oxygen-and-neons-shifting-nuclear-geometry</guid></item><item><title>激光切割铝箔可以取代昂贵的太赫兹偏振器</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/laser-cut-aluminum-foil-could-replace-costly-terahertz-polarizers</link><description>当 ARC 变革元光学系统中心 (TMOS) 的物理学家需要为太赫兹实验提供关键组件时，他们遇到了一个令人沮丧的问题——他们需要微型光学设备，即线栅偏振器，但每个设备的成本高达数千美元。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/laser-cut-aluminum-foil-could-replace-costly-terahertz-polarizers2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 11:17:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/laser-cut-aluminum-foil-could-replace-costly-terahertz-polarizers</guid></item><item><title>新的蒙特卡罗方法加速了密集缠结聚合物熔体的模拟</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/new-monte-carlo-method-accelerates-simulations-of-densely-entangled-polymer-melts</link><description>长聚合物链无处不在：在合成材料、软物质、染色体等生物系统以及细丝和结的数学模型中。当许多这样的链紧密堆积时，它们就会形成物理学家所说的聚合物熔体。在这个拥挤的环境中，每条链都受到周围其他链的限制。这些缠结是聚合物材料行为的核心，但它们也使得系统极难模拟。随着链长度的增加，获得新的独立配置所需的时间增长得非常快。因此，对于非常大的系统，传统的模拟在计算上可能会变得令人望而却步。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/new-monte-carlo-method-accelerates-simulations-of-densely-entangled-polymer-melts2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 11:02:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/new-monte-carlo-method-accelerates-simulations-of-densely-entangled-polymer-melts</guid></item><item><title>“芯片上的彩虹”可以帮助解锁 6G 网络和量子技术的精确计时</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/rainbow-on-a-chip-could-help-unlock-6g-networks-and-precision-timing-for-quantum-technologies</link><description>&lt;img src="https://politepaul.com/fd/dtDF30237DhP.xml" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 10:47:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/rainbow-on-a-chip-could-help-unlock-6g-networks-and-precision-timing-for-quantum-technologies</guid></item><item><title>“我从椅子上跳下来”——天文学家发现一颗隐藏的恒星绕参宿四运行</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/i-jumped-from-my-chair-astronomers-discover-a-hidden-star-orbiting-betelgeuse</link><description>直接成像揭示了强有力的证据，表明参宿四的轨道是一个质量是太阳两到三倍的伴星。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/i-jumped-from-my-chair-astronomers-discover-a-hidden-star-orbiting-betelgeuse2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 10:32:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/i-jumped-from-my-chair-astronomers-discover-a-hidden-star-orbiting-betelgeuse</guid></item><item><title>JWST 发现一颗“恒星”比任何恒星应有的亮度都要亮 1000 亿倍</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/jwst-finds-a-star-100-billion-times-brighter-than-any-star-should-be</link><description>年轻的宇宙中有些东西像星星一样闪闪发光，这是不可能的。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/jwst-finds-a-star-100-billion-times-brighter-than-any-star-should-be2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 10:17:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/jwst-finds-a-star-100-billion-times-brighter-than-any-star-should-be</guid></item><item><title>科学家将被忽视的芯片层转变为强大的新光源</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/scientists-turn-an-overlooked-chip-layer-into-a-powerful-new-light-source</link><description>曾经被视为仅仅是支撑的一层已经将微型光子芯片转变为强大的新光频率发生器。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/scientists-turn-an-overlooked-chip-layer-into-a-powerful-new-light-source2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 10:02:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/scientists-turn-an-overlooked-chip-layer-into-a-powerful-new-light-source</guid></item></channel></rss>